---
code: K0014
title: Assign To Property
severity: ERROR
since: 0.1.0
category: parse
deprecated: False
tags: [parse, syntax, assignment, record-update, immutability]
description: "Direct assignment to a record or object property is not allowed"
---

Direct property assignment (`obj.field = value`) is not supported in Kura. Values and records are immutable, so fields cannot be mutated in place with `=`.

## Example

This error occurs when attempting to assign directly to a member path on a record or object:

```kura
fn move-right(pos: Point): Point => {
  pos.x = 10
  pos
}
```

## Solution

Use a record update expression (`{ record | field: value }`) to produce a new record with the updated field, or rebind the variable name:

```kura
fn move-right(pos: Point): Point => {
  { pos | x: 10 }
}
```

If you are updating a field relative to its existing value, Kura supports compound update operators inside record updates (such as `+=`, `-=`, `*=`, `/=`, and `%=`):

```kura
fn advance(pos: Point): Point => {
  { pos | x += 10 }
}
```
